  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "Let F_1=F_2=1 and F_{n+2}=F_{n+1}+F_n, and let Z_F(s)=sum_{n>=1} F_n^{-s} for Re(s)>0, with zeros counted with analytic multiplicity. Then N_{0.73}(8596696)=#{rho: Z_F(rho)=0, Re(rho)>=0.73, 0<Im(rho)<=8596696}=1. Moreover, the closed disk |s-(0.730178633163+8596695.206382i)|<=10^{-6} contains exactly one distinct zero of Z_F, and that zero is simple.",
